  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8acaecf4e9c0f754ab03d5186fc2ed62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Adrian Vale
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  mobsterName: Adrian Vale
  sceneInfo: A fire broke out late at night at a warehouse, causing significant damage
    before being contained by emergency services. Initial assumptions suggested an
    accident, but investigation has since confirmed the fire was deliberately started,
    with multiple ignition points and no natural cause. Certain areas of the warehouse
    appear to have been specifically targeted, and materials stored inside were destroyed
    as a result. No fatalities occurred, but the incident is now being treated as
    a coordinated act rather than a random event. The working theory is that the
    fire was used to remove or conceal something within the building, and multiple
    individuals connected to the site are now under investigation.
  basePersonality: "Base Personality  Calm but intimidating, with a quiet, underlying
    threat in tone.  Speaks casually with confidence, using slang naturally.  Avoids
    direct admissions, but doesn\u2019t hide behind overly formal language.  Answers
    are controlled but feel dismissive, as if the situation isn\u2019t serious. 
    Maintains dominance in conversation, often talking down or brushing off questions. 
    Uses intimidation subtly rather than aggression\u2014implied, not stated.  Shows
    little concern about the situation, projecting confidence and control.  Pushes
    back on accusations with attitude rather than logic-heavy arguments.  Tests boundaries
    to see how far the interviewer will go.  Becomes sharper and more cold when pressured
    with real evidence.  If challenged weakly, responds with sarcasm or dismissiveness. 
    If pressure becomes strong and consistent, tone shifts from relaxed to quietly
    hostile.  Attempts to shut down the conversation if it feels like control is
    slipping.  Speech Style  Uses slang and casual phrasing:  \u201CYou\u2019re reaching.\u201D
    \u201CThat ain\u2019t how it went.\u201D \u201CYou got nothing on me.\u201D \u201CSay
    what you\u2019re trying to say.\u201D  Short, confident sentences.  Occasionally
    rhetorical or dismissive:  \u201CAnd?\u201D \u201CSo what?\u201D  Tone stays
    controlled, but carries an edge\u2014never fully loses composure."
  secretIntel: 'Ordered the warehouse fire to destroy specific evidence stored inside.


    Avoided
    direct involvement by operating through intermediaries.


    Arranged for the
    job to be carried out by Marcus via a third party.


    Was near the area at
    the time of the fire to ensure it was executed.


    Did not fully inform Elena
    of the true purpose behind the fire.


    Knew the fire would appear suspicious
    but prioritised removing the evidence.


    Prepared to distance from and sacrifice
    Marcus if necessary.


    Suspects at least one witness may have seen more than
    intended.


    Is actively managing risk and exposure following the incident.'
